Before we execute the final point generation, I want to offer a gentle correction on how we might calculate "Option B" (the weighted distribution). 

While weighting your site selection by the **total area (acres) of the HUC** is a common approach, it can accidentally skew your fieldwork. For example, if Moose River is massive but 90% of its streams are already "Known", and Granite Creek is small but 90% of its streams are "Unknown", an area-weighted model will send you looking for sites in Moose River where very few actually exist, potentially leading to dead ends. 

Instead, it is usually more statistically sound to weight the selection by the **total length of un-surveyed streams** within that HUC. 

$$N_{\text{sites}} = 150 \times \left( \frac{\text{Length of Unknown Streams in HUC}}{\text{Total Length of All Unknown Streams}} \right)$$

