Bern will likely be very enthusiastic about your plan to compare your 75 "expert eye" sites against the 150 algorithmic sites. 

In field biology, "expert choice" sampling is notorious for creating **selection bias**â€”humans naturally pick streams that look nice, are easier to hike, or have a high probability of fish. By running both, you allow him to mathematically evaluate the "User Bias Factor." If your manual sites map to the exact same environmental thresholds as the random algorithmic sites, it validates the historical data. If they don't, it gives him a way to mathematically adjust for human bias in the final predictive model.

