### The Strategy: Leverage NetMap's Network Attributes

In standard hydrography, a single river channel can have multiple tributaries join it, but a single channel identifier cannot split as it moves upstream. NetMap data natively includes an attribute designed exactly for thisâ€”usually named **`MS_ID`** (Mainstem ID), **`Stream_ID`**, or **`Channel_ID`**. 

In NetMap's topology, one of those two forks is designated as the continuation of the main channel, while the other fork is assigned a completely unique ID as a new tributary. By telling ArcGIS to look at this attribute during the dissolve phase, the forks will remain completely separate.

