This Quarto (`.qmd`) document establishes a reproducible, automated data pipeline to generate field sampling locations for predicting anadromous fish habitat extent. When calibrating tree-based machine learning algorithms (e.g., Random Forests) to identify Upper Limits of Occupancy (ULO) or Last Fish Observed (LFO), field data must accurately capture the complete distribution of critical landscape covariates, such as channel gradient, drainage basin area, and elevation profiles. 

Rather than standard spatial random samplingâ€”which heavily biases site selection toward low-elevation, dense valley-bottom river systemsâ€”this pipeline executes a **Stratified Proportional Random Sampling Scheme**. By clustering geographic units (e.g., Hydrologic Unit Codes [HUCs]) into distinct landscape strata and allocating site quotas proportionally based on true channel density, the resulting field plan remains statistically sound, landscape-representative, and completely free of manual selection bias.

