## 2. Global Configuration Control Panel

To ensure this script remains entirely adaptive to alternative geographies, river basins, or shifting target metrics, all key criteria are isolated in this initialization block. No downstream code requires manual adjustment.

```{r setup-parameters}
#| label: config
#| message: false

# Load required geospatial and data manipulation libraries
library(sf)
library(tidyverse)

# ---- GLOBAL USER SETTINGS ----
TARGET_SAMPLE_SIZE   <- 150    # Total target field sites to generate
GRADIENT_BARRIER_MAX <- 0.20   # Natural gradient limit (e.g., 20% slope waterfall threshold)
STREAM_ID_COL        <- "CHAN_ID" # Attribute identifying unique continuous channel mainstems

# Define the category field to guide landscape stratification
# (This script dynamically accepts any categorical field, e.g., 'Elevation_Class', 'Stream_Order')
STRATIFICATION_FIELD <- "Elevation_Class"

# Set a random number generator seed to ensure spatial sampling reproducibility
SET_RANDOM_SEED      <- 42
```

